<article class="env-lemma" id="0ET4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ET4">Lemma <span data-tag="0ET4">93.8.6</span>.</a> In Example <a href="/tag/0DY1" data-tag="0DY1">93.8.1</a> assume $P$ is a finite type $k$-algebra such that $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(P) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ is smooth except at a finite number of points. Assume $\Lambda $ is a complete local ring with residue field $k$ (the classical case). Then the functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  F : \mathcal{C}_\Lambda \longrightarrow \textit{Sets},\quad A \longmapsto \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_ P(A))/\cong  \]
</div>
  <p> of isomorphism classes of objects has a hull. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Lemmas <a href="/tag/0DY2" data-tag="0DY2">93.8.2</a> and <a href="/tag/0DY4" data-tag="0DY4">93.8.5</a> and Formal Deformation Theory, Lemma <a href="/tag/06J7" data-tag="06J7">90.16.6</a> and Remark <a href="/tag/06IZ" data-tag="06IZ">90.15.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>